      "message": "`vma_file_offset_at()` returns a signed `loff_t` (`long long`) computed via `((loff_t)vma-\u003evm_pgoff \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL) + ...`. If a driver or character device uses an unsigned 64-bit `mmap` offset cookie with bit 63 set (`ksys_mmap_pgoff()` shifts `(unsigned long)off \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB`, so `vm_pgoff` has bit 49 set), `(loff_t)vma-\u003evm_pgoff \u003c\u003c 14` overflows signed `loff_t` into a negative value and `\u003e\u003e mm_pte_shift(vma-\u003evm_mm)` performs an arithmetic right shift that sign-extends the top 12 bits (`63:52`) to `0xfff`.\n\nComputing directly in unsigned `pgoff_t` avoids the signed byte-shift overflow and acts as the exact lossless inverse of `mm_mmap_pgoff()` / `mm_mmap_slice_off()`:\n```c\nif (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma) \u0026\u0026 vma-\u003evm_file)\n\treturn (vma-\u003evm_pgoff \u003c\u003c P3S_SLICE_SHIFT) + vma_slice_off(vma) +\n\t       ((addr - vma-\u003evm_start) \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB);\n```",
